{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church","id":1047168,"title":"[Dark Eras] Lancea et Sanctum and Church","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-11T05:35:21-08:00","id":1047168,"title":"[Dark Eras] Lancea et Sanctum and Church","content":"I slowly prepare <b>Werewolf</b> chronicle about Vikings raids on Christian monasteries. <b>Dark Eras</b> chapter <i>Wolf and Raven</i> mentions small vampires groups in those cloisters. I suppose most would be Lance Sanctum Kindred, but there rose question - <b>How vampires can live in monastery</b><b>, with it's life so depending on day schedule? </b>Masses and day work are made... well, in daylight, rather than at night. I think that brothers would quickly found out that 2 or 3 of them are missing every activity in monastery. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T07:13:16-08:00","id":1047191,"title":"","content":"How much does your average monks travel? I mean, if your local monastery has monks who only appear at night and that's the only monastery you know, who are you to tell them they're wrong, especially when the ghoul abbot tells you it's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T07:31:39-08:00","id":1047199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047191#post1047191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much does your average monks travel?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Let's assume even that practicaly none, with maybe guest monks once or twice a year,</b> but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047191#post1047191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if your local monastery has monks who only appear at night and that's the only monastery you know, who are you to tell them they're wrong, especially when the ghoul abbot tells you it's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>We have few dozens of brothers in monastery. Two or three are always missing during the day, showing only on supper - and still not <i>really</i> eating.</b> I undestand that 'Brother Abbot approves' can be solution to some groups, but sooner or later <b><i>other</i></b> brothers <i>will</i> notice.<br /> <br /> And solution of 'Brother Thomas is constantly weak on body' seems not working in the long run. Especially as brothers become suddenly lethargic... ( Because one of vampires is more hungry than needing. )<br /> <br /> And Blood Bonding everyone in monastery seems to much to look after - AND Vitea ineffective. You would need to spend 1 Vitea each day for each brother. If monastery would have like 30-50 brothers, it would mean drinking up dry at least 4-5 of them <i>each day</i> to sustain Masquerade! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Maybe Lance Sanctum has some Theban Magic to better pass their priests as flock they should walk inside?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T08:20:13-08:00","id":1047223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047199#post1047199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I undestand that 'Brother Abbot approves' can be solution to some groups, but sooner or later <b><i>other</i></b> brothers <i>will</i> notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less about people noticing, it's more people doing anything about it. I mean, the Abbot isn't an elected leader. There's that one monk who you never see during the day and the Abbot gives him special dispensation to not not be around during the day. It isn't the average monks place to question that.<br /> <br /> The alternative is prehaps a more active cultivation of a cult or herd structure. That doesn't have to mean changing the religion or the function, but actively pulling monks into complicity with the vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T10:06:36-08:00","id":1047289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047199#post1047199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Blood Bonding everyone in monastery seems to much to look after - AND Vitea ineffective. You would need to spend 1 Vitea each day for each brother. If monastery would have like 30-50 brothers, it would mean drinking up dry at least 4-5 of them <i>each day</i> to sustain Masquerade! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One drop works for a year.<br /> <br /> But if they are interested in keeping their identity secret, they would only bond the head of the monastery and a couple others. If for some reason they decided to announce their presence and pretend to be a real priest, they would use powers to support a lie about some sort of disease or something that requires them to keep private.<br /> <br /> It's also entirely within the realms of possibility that such a vampire would have fledgling vampires with them, splitting up the burden of spending Vitae as they teach their coterie. Even Thascius Hostilinus had his three, at least, childer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T11:43:40-08:00","id":1047339,"title":"","content":"Why does the vampire have to be masquerading as a monk? Laity also live in the monastery, lay brothers work the bellows and the farms and clean and keep the candles burning. Why not have the vampire masquerade as one of them instead? Alternatively, give them Obfuscation and they haunt the monastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T13:06:41-08:00","id":1047367,"title":"","content":"You could have the vampire just Obfuscate their way around, passing unseen or unnoticed through the halls. Another fun option could be to have them be the head of the monastery and cultivate all of them as their herd.<br /> <br /> There's also always messing with someone's memories with Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T13:48:28-08:00","id":1047381,"title":"","content":"As someone who plays Meket by preference my thought process tends to assume access to Obfuscate. Most clans have a discipline that can help them hide or make friends (and get donations) so only Gangrel have no easy answer but they don't need a roof over their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T14:35:30-08:00","id":1047397,"title":"","content":"Abbots were usually elected by the other monks. This was hundreds of years before the printing press so it was common work for monks to copy texts so that covers the work aspect for a vampire monk as long as they can manage to stay awake during the day, which is required for the prayers every 3 hours anyway. If they claimed leprosy, I don't think anyone is going to be asking them any questions during that time period. After adding the normal vampire tricks, it seems as easy as a vampire could get at a public lifestyle for the times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T23:05:31-08:00","id":1047572,"title":"","content":"Do not Lancea Sanctum has tenents about leading their mortal flock on religious matters? If yes, then Obfuscate is not solution, as Sanctified need to talk with mortals, so they would be known to monastery community.<br /> <br /> If Blood Bond can last one year on 1 Vitea only, it works much more plausible<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047397#post1047397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abbots were usually elected by the other monks.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how this have anything to the topic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047397#post1047397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was hundreds of years before the printing press so it was common work for monks to copy texts so that covers the work aspect for a vampire monk as long as they can manage to stay awake during the day, which is required for the prayers every 3 hours anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see how coping text is working as good Masquared for vampires. Did it not be better to do this work in the daylight, with, well, light to read text? And do not other copying brothers ( like, I assume, half of monastyr ) would not see you missing your duties every day?<br /> <br /> And you point to other needed condition - You need to show up every 3 hours for prayers - How this could work with day sleeping vampires?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047397#post1047397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they claimed leprosy, I don't think anyone is going to be asking them any questions during that time period.</div> </div> </div> </div>MAYBE it works for Nosferatu, but for other Clans? I heardly see Ventrue or Deava saying 'I'm sick and I will do my things in night' with their obsessions over contact and using Herd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047397#post1047397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After adding the normal vampire tricks, it seems as easy as a vampire could get at a public lifestyle for the times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point me to this 'vampire tricks'? I have only passing knowledge of Requiem mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T00:05:45-08:00","id":1047586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047572#post1047572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not Lancea Sanctum has tenents about leading their mortal flock on religious matters? If yes, then Obfuscate is not solution, as Sanctified need to talk with mortals, so they would be known to monastery community.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they have a strict rule about not worshiping alongside mortals. And they are strong supporters of the Masquerade and the Traditions in general.<br /> <br /> Blood &amp; Smoke, p41, 'The ambivalent relationship of the Sanctified to their living flocks is a case in point. While they have for centuries maintained a strict rule that they do not worship alongside the living, vampiric shepherds do everything they can to make sure these churches survive, pursuing those who would persecute or otherwise harm the living church with terrifying viciousness. On the other hand, the Sanctified believe that they must keep their flocks strong. With fear, a Sanctified monster keeps the wayward children of Mother Church on the straight and narrow: teenagers are terrified into maintaining their virginity by the monsters who hunt at Lovers\u2019 Leap; an abusive priest is fed on, and then driven to suicide; a family is frightened into staying with the church by nightmares and supernatural portents. With temptations, the monsters weed out the weak: A vampire plays on the deep-seated doubts of a nun, driving her to experimentation and addiction, then to prostitution and finally to homelessness and death; a televangelist is given the opportunity to embezzle funds from the Rwandan Orphanage Appeal; a student Bible-group leader is lured to his doom by a beautiful, dark woman. All too often those whom the Sanctified tempt and are found wanting become the next generation of the Sanctified themselves, rising from the grave to atone for the unforgivable.'<br /> <br /> In addition, while the covenant is a religious one, just like the church not every member is a priest. It has its scholars and scribes and other professions in its rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2017, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T00:28:16-08:00","id":1047591,"title":"","content":"So Lancea Sanctum vampires would not attend even night mortal masses in Medieval Church? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T00:37:12-08:00","id":1047593,"title":"","content":"They would to keep an eye on people or screw around with them. They wouldn't to perform their ceremonies, which would likely be perceived as some sort of blasphemy by your average church goer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T01:36:59-08:00","id":1047604,"title":"","content":"Vampires who perform and/or pray along mortals are considered heretics by the central longinian creed. During the midnight masses, longinians are more likely going to prey upon the monks who miss services and sacraments, even if it took a little prompting from them to do so. Untested virtue is not virtue at all for the Lancea et Sanctum, and tempting the self-claimed pure is one of their most basic tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T01:47:00-08:00","id":1047608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047572#post1047572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how this have anything to the topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone suggested using an abbot. Someone else that they were not elected. If you use an abbot, it is important to know that they need the support of most of the monks. It is a complication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not see how coping text is working as good Masquared for vampires. Did it not be better to do this work in the daylight, with, well, light to read text? And do not other copying brothers ( like, I assume, half of monastyr ) would not see you missing your duties every day?<br /> And you point to other needed condition - You need to show up every 3 hours for prayers - How this could work with day sleeping vampires?<br /> MAYBE it works for Nosferatu, but for other Clans? I heardly see Ventrue or Deava saying 'I'm sick and I will do my things in night' with their obsessions over contact and using Herd. </div> </div> </div>Copying text would be an indoor activity often away from windows so avoiding sunlight is possible while doing it. Candle light instead of daylight could be used to see. Vampires can stay awake during the day with difficulty. This would be required to be a monk for the reasons you mention. Lepers were ostracized, that was my point. Nobody would notice minor issues like not eating. Work and prayer would not be minor. A Herd of lepers would be possible. Monks were known to treat the sick and run leper colonies or asylums.<br /> <br /> It is possible but difficult, and I think it would not be fun to play. I think it would be better to have the vampires make some monks servants. Actually, the vampires could claim to be lepers and control a few monks to maintain the ruse. Everyone else would be too busy avoiding them and where they stay to care about what the vampires were doing in their home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you point me to this 'vampire tricks'? I have only passing knowledge of Requiem mechanics. </div> </div> </div>Discipline, blood bond, etc. It is a figure of speech. Don't worry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 02-12-2017, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T04:49:24-08:00","id":1047655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047604#post1047604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires who perform and/or pray along mortals are considered heretics by the central longinian creed. During the midnight masses, longinians are more likely going to prey upon the monks who miss services and sacraments, even if it took a little prompting from them to do so. Untested virtue is not virtue at all for the Lancea et Sanctum, and tempting the self-claimed pure is one of their most basic tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so you tell me that Lancea Sanctum would not work and pray with their mortal congregation?! <br /> <br /> So they do not have reason to stay in monastery in the first place. I'm confused - for years I assumed that playing 'vampire priest' was whole point of this Covenant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T05:01:33-08:00","id":1047658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047655#post1047655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they do not have reason to stay in monastery in the first place. I'm confused - for years I assumed that playing 'vampire priest' was whole point of this Covenant...</div> </div> </div> </div>They watch over the mortal church, they just aren't meant to participate.<br /> <br /> Plus, a monastery has resources that are specifically useful to the LS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T06:23:12-08:00","id":1047672,"title":"","content":"Oh they're still Vampire Priest. They just don't pray and preach directly to mortals. They pray and preach with other undead. <br /> <br /> Notably, the 1st edition book Ancient Mysteries had it that in medieval times the Western Lancea Sanctum still prayed with mortals, and it wasn't until the fall of Constantinople that the Byzantine Kindred practice is separated worship was adopted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T07:14:01-08:00","id":1047686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047672#post1047672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh they're still Vampire Priest. They just don't pray and preach directly to mortals. They pray and preach with other undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This <i>not </i>work with assumption that in medieval times you have like handful of Kindred in one place. Like up too 3 in one monastery ( direct call back to <i>Wolf and Raven</i> chapter ). Who you 'priest' and make Kindred only masses? One child of yours?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047672#post1047672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, the 1st edition book Ancient Mysteries had it that in medieval times the Western Lancea Sanctum still prayed with mortals, and it wasn't until the fall of Constantinople that the Byzantine Kindred practice is separated worship was adopted</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>This</i> works much better!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I understand that Lancea could in later era adopt 'not intermingling with mortals' policy when Kindred numbers risen, but in late Antiquity and early Medieval eras, it just not work with vampires numbers to separate that much on God worship.<br /> <br /> Now only HOW to make Medieval Lancea members to join their mortals flock in prays in day...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2017, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:27:49-08:00","id":1047812,"title":"","content":"A vampire can roll stamina and resolve to stay awake during the day. Without an exceptional success, another roll is required every 6 hours with a penalty for each 6 hours. Another way is to have someone wake up the vampire, if they have high humanity. Lance members are more likely than most to pull it off. It won't be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:42:31-08:00","id":1047821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047812#post1047812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire can roll stamina and resolve to stay awake during the day. Without an exceptional success, another roll is required every 6 hours with a penalty for each 6 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Lancea members will have high Stamina and Resolve, okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1047812#post1047812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way is to have someone wake up the vampire, if they have high humanity. Lance members are more likely than most to pull it off. It won't be easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>HOW Lancea members are more likely to pull it off? I did not envision Covenant members as having high Humanity in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2017, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:51:22-08:00","id":1047827,"title":"","content":"They prefer to have high Humanity. They cling to it, and low Humanity means they can't use their sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:09:16-08:00","id":1048076,"title":"","content":"Should not high Humanity mean that Lancea members be close to mortals? I.E. They should play they role as monk and not 'haunt' the monastries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T03:19:55-08:00","id":1048152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1048076#post1048076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not high Humanity mean that Lancea members be close to mortals? I.E. They should play they role as monk and not 'haunt' the monastries?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a high Humanity means they're very good at pretending to be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T05:02:02-08:00","id":1048184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1048152#post1048152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, a high Humanity means they're very good at pretending to be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hiding yourself in shadows as 'invisible predator' with Obfuscate do not sound as 'being good in pretending to be human'... I think it should be Breaking Point <i>against</i> Humanity if you are reveling in your 'I'm hidden vampire'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:23:45-08:00","id":1048226,"title":"","content":"The first dot of Obfuscate allows you to hide in crowds. You can't directly interact with people without breaking Obfuscate, but you can stand next to a human and observe them in order to (re)gain a better understanding of human lives. Besides, you don't need to have close to maxed Humanity in order to use Theban Sorcery. Humanity 5 is enough to be able to use the full scale of it, while using Obfuscate in that way would be a Breaking Point at Humanity 9 at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:41:06-08:00","id":1048234,"title":"","content":"Being shunned by or avoiding contact with humans IS a Humanity violation with the level commensurate with the duration of separation. Nothing says their relationship MUST entail reducing every human in the vicinity to sycophantic blood addicted sex objects or blood cattle or else they're breaking the Masquerade. The Ventrue Sanctified paladin who adopts the role of forester who shows twice a week and drops off some game and chats with the cook or random friar and uses his powers to deter sectarian schisms within or fighting off incursions by other vampires from preying on the denizens without most certainly qualifies as a protector of the monastery without dictating taking an oath and joining them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T08:09:18-08:00","id":1048247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1048184#post1048184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiding yourself in shadows as 'invisible predator' with Obfuscate do not sound as 'being good in pretending to be human'... I think it should be Breaking Point <i>against</i> Humanity if you are reveling in your 'I'm hidden vampire'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? You're directly interacting with humans constantly, you're watching them live their normal lives. You're probably getting invested in them, too, they are 'yours' and you would protect them if you had to. They might even warrant being a Touchstone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T08:53:22-08:00","id":1048260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1047168-dark-eras-lancea-et-sanctum-and-church?p=1048247#post1048247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? You're directly interacting with humans constantly, you're watching them live their normal lives. You're probably getting invested in them, too, they are 'yours' and you would protect them if you had to. They might even warrant being a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that 'watching over from shadows' is the same way 'directly interacting' like stalking someone is being with that one in relationship...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:05:20-08:00","id":1048263,"title":"","content":"And that's totally fine for vampires. Humanity is not about acting like a good human. It's about being grounded and reminded of humans so you won't turn into a mindless predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:35:30-08:00","id":1048281,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> Vampires are undead monsters.<br /> <br /> Their Humanity is a ticking clock waiting for them to finally act like one.<br /> <br /> Clinging to Humanity does not mean acting like a human, or a good person, it's clinging to the last vestiges of what you were, even if that means only watching it from a distance.<br /> <br /> Besides, even if the vampire is lurking around with Obfuscate, that doesn't mean they can't pick a mortal to associate with in private.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2017, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:44:56-08:00","id":1048288,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see a totally separate christianity-styles Covenant that preaches salvation for the Damned and specifically struggle against becoming the monsters that L+S preaches it's their divine duty to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T22:02:25-08:00","id":1053636,"title":"","content":"I would point out that any group that considers a Vow of Silence normal is likely to accept all sorts of strangeness (I swore a vow never to stand in sunlight least others seeing my face lead to vanity). Also the further the monastery is from the Mother Church in Rome the more likely aberrant practices and even beliefs are to arise among its members. It was common for frontier churches to mix pagan practices into their worship, just dress it up in orthodoxy and you now have Saint Thor, patron saint of storms.<br /> This is why the Guttenberg Bible was such a big deal, like Webster's Dictionary it created a common source of reference that didn't change. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 02-23-2017, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T21:04:29-08:00","id":1056968,"title":"","content":"No one knows who takes the night time confessional at St Augustine's Abby, its a matter of idle speculation and rumour amongst the brothers in fact. Its always the same person, that same pair of piercing eyes just visible behind the screen, that same velvety and inviting voice with its dulcet meter, that same aura that arouses unrestrained candour. Nobody really takes confession during the day anymore.<br /> <br /> Try as you might you'll never see the mysterious confessor enter the booth, nor will you see them leave. Accepted thought says that there must be some concealed means of egress and entrance; a cunningly hidden secret passage behind a wooden panel. Brother Jacob once spent hours inside trying to find the hidden door to no avail, the abbot was wroth when he caught him and set him harsh penance for his curiosity. Its definitely not the Abbot though, once as I exited the booth after taking the sacrament I observed that the abbot was lighting candles and only the holy spirit may be in two places at once.<br /> <br /> Most times the Unknown Confessor speaks very little outside the ritual of the sacrament, Instead letting their palpable acceptance and the weight of one's sins to steer us back into the arms and forgiveness of the Lord. Sometimes however it isn't content simply to listen, these times it ask questions. Not merely of the details of the sins volunteered for which one's seeks contrition but of other and darker things. Sinister, blasphemous things imagined and hypothetical but heretical and disturbing in nature. You can always tell when a brother has had one of those confessionals. They all vary in reaction but there is a shared look as if they have been struck to the very quick and core of their being.<br /> <br /> Brother Aldous had that look when he emerged two weeks ago. He spent the rest of the night sobbing and begging before the Virgin Mary, Ignoring the others who sought to aid him in his distress. Afterwards he refused to sleep at night, napping only briefly in between day prayers which he attended with frenzied devotion. The last thing that he told me, in a breathless and fearful whisper, was that the Confessor knew what we had done together. We found him dead in the middle of the cloister the morning after with no mark on him but a single cold tear on his cheek. I haven't been to confession since. The others have all begun to notice. I can no longer avoid it though the idea fills me with terrifying thrills. <br /> <br /> Tonight I give my confession.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bsorry i just had to...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T00:19:27-08:00","id":1057013,"title":"","content":"I wondering - What have narrator and Brother Aldous done together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:55:19-08:00","id":1057088,"title":"","content":"I have no idea, cant say I thought overly hard on it, I leave it entirely to the readers choice and interpretation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T22:07:29-07:00","id":1116726,"title":"","content":"As I plan to run this abbey story next, I come to verify my ideas. It will be monastery at Isle Iona in 799, few years after famous Lindisfarne raid. Abby is mostly typical 'copying center' run by Abbot. He says they have small lepers colony that help in their godly mission. In reality, those are Lancea Sanctum vampires from Nosferatu Clan - Elder Sire and his two Children. Officially, lepers are running night masses past dusk, to 'not grief God with their visage'. Abbot is Blood Bonded by Sire and all Nosferatu are feding on monks and nearby peasants that break Ten Commandments. Does this sound pluasable in Requiem setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-16-2017, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}